<Base
  title="How compound interest works: the formula, worked examples and the rule of 72"
  description="Compound interest is interest on interest: $10,000 at 7% a year becomes $76,123 in 30 years, against $31,000 on simple interest. The formula, a year-by-year table, monthly deposits, and the rule of 72, all worked by hand."
